<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<!--
  Vanilla Expanded. This is the file the port changed.

  MysticFelines wrote it against six Vanilla Expanded mods. Three of them cannot load in 1.6:

    Vanilla Factions Expanded - Ancients   VanillaExpanded.VFEA
        last updated 27 May 2025, tagged 1.3/1.4/1.5, no 1.6 folder on disk.
        VFEA_AncientChemfuelPoweredGenerator and VFEA_FueledMendingStation exist nowhere else.
        Both operations dropped.

    [1.4] Vanilla Factions Expanded - Medieval   OskarPotocki.VanillaFactionsExpanded.MedievalModule
        The Workshop title now begins with the version, which is how the Vanilla Expanded team
        marks a module it has stopped. Its content moved to Medieval 2, where the only lit
        furniture is the hearth and its darklight twin - the candle and the wall torch lamp did
        not make the move. VFEM_Candle and VFEM_WallTorchLamp dropped.

    Vanilla Expanded - Royalty Patches / Ideology Patches
        last updated 8 March 2024, tagged up to 1.4. These defined VFEM_DarkCandle,
        VFEM_WallTorchDarkLamp and VFEV_DarkHearth - the darklight variants of Medieval's and
        Vikings' furniture. The first two are gone with Medieval 1. The third has a successor,
        below.

  One retarget. VFEV_DarkHearth was the Ideology twin of the Vikings hearth, and [1.4] Vanilla
  Factions Expanded - Vikings is dead too. Both hearths were folded into Medieval 2, where the
  plain one is VFEM2_Hearth and the darklight one VFEM2_HearthDarklight, carrying the same
  refuelable / glower / heat pusher comps it had as VFEV_DarkHearth. The operation follows it
  there, keeping MysticFelines' particleSize and gaining one field - an indoorAlt, one of the
  three this file adds; see the note on the operation itself. VFEM2_HearthDarklight
  sits behind Medieval 2's
  Ideology load folder, so it is absent without the DLC - which the conditional handles, the same
  way it handles Medieval 2 not being installed at all.

  One typo removed. The source had two operations for the Medieval dark candle, one of which
  tested for VVFEM_DarkCandle - two Vs - while adding to VFEM_DarkCandle. PatchOperationConditional
  runs <match> only when its own xpath matches, so that operation had never fired since it was
  written. It is moot now, since the def it aimed at is gone either way, but it is worth recording
  that it was dead on arrival rather than killed by 1.6.

  Two survive unchanged, both verified against 1.6 defs on disk:

    VFEC_HeatStones, VFEC_WoodFiredCrematorium   Vanilla Factions Expanded - Classical, 1.6
    Stone_DarklightCampfire                      Vanilla Furniture Expanded, 1.6/Mods/Ideology

  The last one was filed under "VE Ideology Patches + VFE Core" in the source. It is neither: it
  is Vanilla Furniture Expanded's own dark firepit, in the folder its loadfolders.xml loads with
  IfModActive="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology". The mod is alive and the def is unchanged, so the
  operation stands as written - only the comment was wrong.

  Every conditional also carries [not(comps/li[@Class="Flecker.CompProperties_Smoker"])].
  Patches apply in mod load order and this mod loads after Simple FX: Smoke, so its comps are
  already in the document when these run. If it ever adds one of these buildings to its own
  patches, the operation here stands down instead of adding a second comp and doubling the
  smoke - a collision a defName test cannot see, because the def exists either way.
-->
<Patch>

  <!-- Vanilla Factions Expanded - Classical -->

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="VFEC_HeatStones"][not(comps/li[@Class="Flecker.CompProperties_Smoker"])]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="VFEC_HeatStones"]/comps</xpath>
      <value>
        <li Class="Flecker.CompProperties_Smoker">
          <fleckDef>Owl_SmokeIndoors</fleckDef>
          <particleSize>1</particleSize>
        </li>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <!-- indoorAlt added; MysticFelines left it off. Simple FX: Smoke's own ElectricCrematorium has
       exactly this shape - billsOnly, particleSize 1 - and carries indoorAlt, and so does the
       chemfuel crematorium in this mod's own Appliances Expanded file. Not unanimous, in
       fairness: upstream's CoalCrematorium has none either. -->

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="VFEC_WoodFiredCrematorium"][not(comps/li[@Class="Flecker.CompProperties_Smoker"])]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="VFEC_WoodFiredCrematorium"]/comps</xpath>
      <value>
        <li Class="Flecker.CompProperties_Smoker">
          <billsOnly>true</billsOnly>
          <particleSize>1</particleSize>
          <indoorAlt>Owl_SmokeIndoors</indoorAlt>
        </li>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <!-- Vanilla Factions Expanded - Medieval 2.

       New coverage, and the one place this mod goes beyond MysticFelines' list. Simple FX: Smoke
       patches VFEV_Hearth, the Vikings hearth - a defName that cannot exist in 1.6, because
       [1.4] Vanilla Factions Expanded - Vikings does not load there. It did not follow the
       building into Medieval 2, so VFEM2_Hearth is covered by nobody, while its darklight twin
       below is covered here. A player with Medieval 2 and Ideology would see one hearth smoke
       and the other not.

       The values are the upstream ones for VFEV_Hearth, read out of Simple FX: Smoke's own
       AddSmokeVE.xml, not invented: particleSize 1.5 and indoorAlt Owl_SmokeIndoors. -->

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="VFEM2_Hearth"][not(comps/li[@Class="Flecker.CompProperties_Smoker"])]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="VFEM2_Hearth"]/comps</xpath>
      <value>
        <li Class="Flecker.CompProperties_Smoker">
          <particleSize>1.5</particleSize>
          <indoorAlt>Owl_SmokeIndoors</indoorAlt>
        </li>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <!-- Vanilla Factions Expanded - Medieval 2, with Ideology.
       Was VFEV_DarkHearth in [1.4] Vanilla Factions Expanded - Vikings.

       indoorAlt added; MysticFelines gave this operation particleSize 1.5 and no indoorAlt. The
       two hearths are the same building in two variants, they sit indoors, and without it this
       one kept the heavy outdoor fleck in a room while its plain twin switched to the light
       indoor one. Owlchemist made the same call on the same building: VFEV_Hearth carries
       indoorAlt in Simple FX: Smoke's own file, and so does MysticFelines' own DarklightBrazier.

       This is one of THREE values in this mod that are not as their author left them - the other
       two are on VFEC_WoodFiredCrematorium and Stone_DarklightCampfire above and below. All
       three are the same field for the same reason. Tabulating the twenty operations shows the
       rule MysticFelines follows: indoorAlt goes with the default heavy Smoke fleck, and is left
       off wherever fleckDef is already Owl_Vapor, which needs no lighter indoor variant.

       Three operations sit outside that rule and are RIGHT to. BurnPit uses the heavy fleck with
       no indoorAlt, but a burn pit is an outdoor building with nothing indoors to switch to.
       VFEC_HeatStones sets Owl_SmokeIndoors as its main fleckDef - the indoor form is the only
       form it ever uses, so an alternate would be pointless. CA_ChemfuelTurbine uses
       Owl_SmokeHeavy, whose indoor twin is Owl_SmokeHeavyIndoors rather than Owl_SmokeIndoors:
       a real fourth candidate, but it needs a different value from these three, it was not part
       of what was asked, and it is left alone rather than guessed at. -->

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="VFEM2_HearthDarklight"][not(comps/li[@Class="Flecker.CompProperties_Smoker"])]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="VFEM2_HearthDarklight"]/comps</xpath>
      <value>
        <li Class="Flecker.CompProperties_Smoker">
          <particleSize>1.5</particleSize>
          <indoorAlt>Owl_SmokeIndoors</indoorAlt>
        </li>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <!-- Vanilla Furniture Expanded, with Ideology.

       indoorAlt added; MysticFelines left it off. This is the hearth case again, and the clearest
       of the three: Stone_DarklightCampfire is the Ideology twin of Stone_Campfire, which Simple
       FX: Smoke patches with particleSize 1.5 AND indoorAlt Owl_SmokeIndoors - the same size, one
       field more. So did vanilla's own Campfire. The two firepits sit side by side in the same
       build menu and had no reason to smoke differently indoors. -->

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="Stone_DarklightCampfire"][not(comps/li[@Class="Flecker.CompProperties_Smoker"])]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="Stone_DarklightCampfire"]/comps</xpath>
      <value>
        <li Class="Flecker.CompProperties_Smoker">
          <particleSize>1.5</particleSize>
          <indoorAlt>Owl_SmokeIndoors</indoorAlt>
        </li>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
